# The Friday weekly review: a headless Claude Code run.
# Read by scripts/gen_launchd.py.

[job]
name = weekly
exit_timeout = 1800
run_at_load = false
stdin = {ROOT}/config/prompts/weekly_review.md

[program]
{CLAUDE}
-p
--permission-mode
acceptEdits
--allowedTools
Read Glob Grep Write Edit WebFetch Bash(git add:*) Bash(git commit:*) Bash(git status:*) Bash(git diff:*) Bash(git log:*)

[environment]
TZ = America/New_York
PATH = {HOME}/.local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin
HOME = {HOME}
AGENTIC_TRADING_ROOT = {ROOT}

[schedule]
# 4:45 PM Eastern on Friday, fifteen minutes after the last learning loop of the
# week, so the week's final journal entry already exists when this reads it.
at 16:45 on friday

[comment]
The weekly review, run by launchd.

At 16:45 Eastern on Fridays it starts Claude Code with no terminal attached and
feeds it the prompt at {ROOT}/config/prompts/weekly_review.md on standard input.
Claude reads the ledger's Books tab, the week's journal entries and last week's
review, and writes {ROOT}/docs/weekly/YYYY-WW.md comparing the five books on
return, alpha versus SPY, drawdown, trades, commissions, model cost, rule
triggers and missed ticks, then says what to carry into next week.

It runs fifteen minutes after Friday's daily learning loop on purpose, so the
week's last journal entry is already written when this one starts reading.

WHAT IT IS ALLOWED TO DO. Reading, writing files, fetching the ledger sheet, and
a short list of git commands. It cannot run the trading loop, cannot reach IB
Gateway or the MCP server, and cannot place an order.

WHAT IT NEEDS. The same as the learning loop: Claude Code installed and signed in
as Mo, and the Mac logged in to the desktop. It also needs the Google token at
{ROOT}/.secrets/token_personal_drive.json to read the ledger.

If nothing appears in {ROOT}/docs/weekly/ after a Friday, read
{ROOT}/output/launchd_weekly.err.log first.
